      {
        "question_text": "A recipe uses $3$ cups of stock for $8$ serves.\n(a) How many cups are needed for $32$ serves?\n(b) How many serves can be made with $21$ cups?",
        "solution_text": "Use whole recipe batches. Each batch makes $8$ serves using $3$ cups.\n(a) $32\\div8=4$ batches.\n$3\\times4=12$ cups.\n(b) $21\\div3=7$ batches.\n$8\\times7=56$ serves. Keep the cups and serves in their own groups."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Six identical admission tickets cost $\\$138$.\n(a) At the same rate, how much do $9$ tickets cost?\n(b) How many tickets can be bought for $\\$345$?",
        "solution_text": "First find the cost of one ticket: $\\$138\\div6=\\$23$.\n(a) Find the total by multiplying: $\\$23\\times9=\\$207$.\n(b) Find the number of tickets by dividing: $\\$345\\div\\$23=15$ tickets."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A bus travels $228$ km in $4$ hours at a steady rate.\n(a) How far does it travel in $7$ hours?\n(b) How many hours does it take to travel $342$ km?",
        "solution_text": "Find the distance travelled in one hour: $228\\div4=57$ km.\n(a) Multiply the hourly distance by the time: $57\\times7=399$ km.\n(b) Divide the distance by the hourly distance: $342\\div57=6$ hours."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A machine labels $72$ jars every $3$ minutes at a steady rate. How many jars does it label in $20$ minutes?",
        "solution_text": "The given block is $3$ minutes. Find the one-minute amount: $72\\div3=24$ jars.\nThen multiply by $20$ minutes: $24\\times20=480$ jars. Dividing first gives a whole-number rate even though $20$ is not a multiple of $3$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A workshop must make $1560$ parts. A machine makes $65$ parts per hour and has run for $14$ hours. How many more hours are needed?",
        "solution_text": "Find how many parts have already been made: $65\\times14=910$ parts.\nParts remaining $=1560-910=650$.\nDivide the remaining amount by the hourly rate: $650\\div65=10$ more hours. The question asks for extra time, not the total time."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A bottling machine fills $54$ bottles every $3$ minutes at a steady rate. How many bottles does it fill in $12$ minutes?",
        "solution_text": "Find the number of three-minute blocks: $12\\div3=4$ blocks.\nEach block produces $54$ bottles: $54\\times4=216$ bottles."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A bus travels $192$ km in $4$ hours, then continues for $3$ more hours at the same steady rate. What total distance does it travel?",
        "solution_text": "Find the distance travelled in one hour: $192\\div4=48$ km.\nCombine the consecutive time periods: $4+3=7$ hours altogether.\nMultiply the hourly distance by the total time: $48\\times7=336$ km."
      }
    ],
